title: "QQL documentation"
description: "Learn the Qdrant Query Language and use the same typed query surface from Rust, Python, Node.js, WebAssembly, and the QQL CLI."
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

QQL is a typed, declarative language for Qdrant. It turns search, hybrid
retrieval, mutations, collection management, and tenant-safe policies into one
portable syntax.

{% grid style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap:1rem;" %}

{% glassCard title="One language" %}
{% techBadge name="qql-core" variant="cyan" /%}

The canonical grammar, typed AST, strict full-script parser, validation, and
filter injection are shared by every SDK.
{% /glassCard %}

{% glassCard title="One plan" %}
{% techBadge name="qql-plan" variant="purple" /%}

Statements lower to a transport-neutral plan before REST, gRPC, or in-process
edge dispatch.
{% /glassCard %}

{% glassCard title="Every host" %}
{% techBadge name="Rust" variant="orange" /%} {% techBadge name="Python" variant="purple" /%}

Use native Rust, Python, Node.js, WebAssembly, or the `qql` command-line tool
without learning another query dialect.
{% /glassCard %}

{% glassCard title="Policy at the AST" %}
{% techBadge name="Fail closed" variant="cyan" /%}

Parse untrusted QQL, recursively inject mandatory filters, then plan and
execute the rewritten statement.
{% /glassCard %}

{% /grid %}

## A first query

{% qqlExample title="Semantic nearest-neighbor search" %}
```sql
QUERY 'vector database'
FROM docs
USING dense
WHERE status = 'published'
WITH PAYLOAD INCLUDE (title, url)
LIMIT 10;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

This source remains readable in a pull request, a support ticket, or a browser
session. Open it in the playground to see the AST and the Qdrant request before
choosing a backend.

